    "title": "Which Arizona grocery stores are open on Easter? See holiday hours",
    "text": "April 3, 2026Updated April 5, 2026, 5:01 a.m. MTEaster Sunday falls on April 5 this year. Lamb, deviled eggs, hot cross buns, ham, spring vegetables: whatever Easter goodies you have planned for the holiday, it's highly likely you might need to make a last-minute run to the grocery store.Before doing so, it's worth checking which stores are open on Easter Sunday. Some have their regular hours, while others are closed entirely. To make shopping easier, The Arizona Republic put together a guide to the Easter hours of major retailers, from Walmart to Fry's.Aldi, Costco and Target are the only stores that will be closed—the rest are open for full or partial hours. Here's what to know.AJ's Fine Foods Easter hoursAJ's will be open on Easter from 6 a.m. to 7 p.m.Aldi Easter hoursAldi grocery stores will be closed on Easter.Bashas' Easter hoursBashas' will be open on Easter from 6 a.m. to 7 p.m.Costco Easter hoursCostco warehouses will be closed on Easter.Get the latest grocery news with Attention Shoppers, our weekly newsletter. Food City Easter hoursFood City locations will be open until 7 p.m. on Easter.Fry's Christmas hoursFry's will be open its usual hours on Easter.Sprouts Easter hoursSprouts will be open for its usual hours on Easter.Target Easter hoursTarget will be closed on Easter.Trader Joe's Easter hoursTrader Joe's will be open for its usual hours on Easter.Walmart Supercenter Easter hoursWalmart stores will be open for their regular hours on Easter.Whole Foods Easter hoursWhole Foods will be open from 7 a.m. to 6 p.m. on Easter.WinCo Foods Easter hoursWinCo will be open its usual 24 hours on Easter.Reach the reporter at reia.li@gannett.com. Follow @reia_reports on Instagram.",
